      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T17:34:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the absence of a hypervisor at EL2, the interface between EL1 and EL3 would be the non-secure physical instance. Similarly, with VHE then the host would be running entirely at EL2 and would be using the non-secure physical instance.\n\nGiven that we\u0027re trapping SMCs from the host, rather than handling HVCs, then I tend to think of the EL2 code as a shim/proxy rather than an active FFA participant, and so I would still consider the host to be using the non-secure physical instance.\n\nIt\u0027s certainly not clear-cut, however, as we\u0027re using separate RXTX buffer pairs, so I\u0027m happy to change the comment (or remove it entirely), Do you have a better wording?",
      "parentUuid": "e18a2674_f8966d3b",
